WEBVTT

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:08.940
The Stagiaire requires participants to leave a visible mark in a professional setting.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:13.740
The challenge was reaching its zenith.{technically doesn't need an8 but subs moving around too much is dumb}

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.110
No, no!

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:16.950
That's not how you time the suer process!{no reference to suer anywhere}

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:18.370
Watch.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:19.590
Don't rush.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:21.410
Cook as though you're 
making the vegetables sweat.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.120
Here.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.360
Don't forget what this surface looks like right here.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.080
Got it.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.800
French cuisine is really interesting.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:34.470
It uses a completely different thought process from traditional Japanese cuisine.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:35.680
You're right.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.770
Japanese cuisine tends to emphasize

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.220
minimal handling and processing of ingredients to keep them "raw,"

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:44.230
but French cuisine spends copious amounts
 of time and effort on processing ingredients.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:48.540
Even making a single stock 
requires an extremely long time.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.400
It's entirely different from, say, the use of dried bonito in Japanese cuisine—

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.120
What?

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:56.030
Oh, just thinking that you're a really good teacher.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:58.780
That's because you have zero basic knowledge of French cuisine!

00:00:58.780 --> 00:00:59.740
Do you even get that?

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:00.180
Sure.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.080
Yukihira, have you memorized the recette for the fish dish today?

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.210
Yup!

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:06.160
I'm all good.

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:09.130
So how's it going, Yukihira?

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:12.880
Did you figure out what you're going to make in tonight's competition?

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.800
Yeah, I have the basic idea,

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.750
but I haven't managed to finalize it, I guess.

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:19.720
Ready?

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:22.430
Don't let your guard down on the last day.

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:22.970
Let's go.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:24.430
Oui, chef!

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:28.270
<i>The specialty... a dish that I alone can make...</i>

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:31.450
<i>I'll make it tonight for sure!</i>

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:56.630
Far beyond the image I have in my mind

00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:03.100
The reality I'm building up is still far away

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.850
An endless journey

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:11.860
Let's hone each other's pride

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.360
Words aren't really important

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:16.860
So let's just say "yes" and leave it at that

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:23.830
We fight each other and hone our skills

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.710
Our encounters cause shockwaves

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:31.460
We're reckless challengers

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:36.460
Heading toward a world as yet unexplored

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.010
A swordsman should use his blade

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:41.840
To open the way to the future

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:47.560
This is my story and no one else's

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:09.680
Chef Shinomiya, the pre-open at SHINO's Tokyo is a huge success!

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:11.260
Do you have plans for a third restaurant?

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:13.880
Let's not get ahead of ourselves.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:19.970
I first have to make SHINO's Tokyo as established as my flagship restaurant in Paris.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.550
Yukihira, next up is Table 3! Hurry!

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:24.180
Got it.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.510
Yukihira, I need help here too.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:28.210
Table 6 will be showing up late.

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:30.770
Then I'll work on the fish dish for Table 5 first.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:33.940
Thank you.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.560
Please take care.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.360
Well, I guess the pre-open's finally done.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:44.590
So you only close this early
 when it's the last day of the pre-open.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.370
We're not closed yet.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.830
I've invited one more group of guests
 and reserved the whole place for them.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:52.370
Evening!

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.370
Oh, Yukihira-kun?

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:55.480
Why are you here?

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.590
Oh, I'm here for the Stagiaire!

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:01.100
Jeez, you called Yukihira-kun, but not me?

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:03.360
Why won't you let me help you?

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:05.470
You have your own restaurant, stupid.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.000
It's been a while, everyone.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.350
Yukihira Souma.

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:13.000
I see. So this was your training site.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:13.810
Interesting...

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:16.640
I haven't seen you since the camp.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:18.770
Good work in the Autumn Selection.

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:20.130
Thanks.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:24.910
Chapelle-sensei came to Tohtsuki 
when we were still students there.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:25.660
Huh.

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:28.630
It's been a while, Chapelle-sensei.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:29.760
Cheers to your eyes.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:33.830
Shinomiya Kojirou, you were always full of energy, even as a student.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.370
Thank you.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:32.260
Um... er...

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:33.120
Sorry.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:38.080
You had some fragility to you back then,
 but I see no trace of that now.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.520
I am proud of you.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:41.710
Advance yourself.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:43.170
Thank you.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.380
This way in, please.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.900
I am the head chef for SHINO's Tokyo.

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:49.140
Oh, my. Your staff look like French dolls.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:51.140
Welcome, Madame.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.150
Don't call me that!

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:56.100
Don't tease me, Kojirou.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.520
<i>Shinomiya-senpai's...</i>

00:04:57.520 --> 00:04:58.480
<i>...mother?!</i>

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.400
You're always so selfish!

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:03.490
After years of not even visiting me,
 why'd you invite me out here in Tokyo?!

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.050
I feel bad about that, okay?

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:06.320
That's why I invited you.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.360
I'm not used to coming out to a place like this.

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:09.220
I'm uncomfortable.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:11.430
Just relax.

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.700
That's... Japanese, right?

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:13.050
Make yourself at home.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.710
Wow. I can hardly believe he's the same person.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:15.160
No way!

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.350
Delicious.

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.130
Um, Shinomiya-senpai.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:39.400
I've always wanted to ask this,

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.790
but why did you choose 
to specialize in French cuisine?

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:49.360
<i>It was to celebrate my entrance 
into elementary school.</i>

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:56.280
<i>Just that one time, I went with my parents to a local French restaurant.</i>

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.410
<i>We wore our best clothes</i>

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:01.590
<i>and practiced how to use a knife and fork at home.</i>

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:05.210
<i>Now that I think about it,
 the restaurant wasn't anything special.</i>

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:08.250
Kojirou, isn't this delicious?

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:13.430
I've never had something this good.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:16.010
French food is amazing.

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:21.200
<i>If I become a French chef,</i>

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:24.790
<i>I can make Mom smile all the time...</i>

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:32.730
And why would I tell you?

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:33.870
I thought you might say that.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:34.910
Come along.

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:36.120
It's time to prepare dessert.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:37.330
Oh, sure.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:41.250
About the quiche I made on the first day...

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:43.840
What about it?

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:47.630
Burdock root apparently only looks like a tree root to Westerners.

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:51.990
They're often surprised to learn that Japanese people eat it.

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:52.970
Huh.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:57.030
People have avoided other root vegetables,

00:06:57.030 --> 00:06:59.850
like carrots and parsley root,

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.870
because they bring back memories
 of wartime food shortages.

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:03.860
I see.

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:08.440
The forgotten vegetables: "legumes oubliés."

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:10.490
If I were to name that quiche,

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:13.740
I'd call it Quiche de légumes oubliés, I guess.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:15.820
<i>There have to be dishes that only I can make,</i>

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:20.080
<i>having experienced both 
French and Japanese cultures.</i>

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.130
You asked me before

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:25.340
why I chose to open 
a restaurant in Japan right now.

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:25.840
Yes.

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:30.220
It's to reaffirm what the roots of my cooking are.

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:31.590
Roots...

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:35.600
I'm going to face my own cooking in the country
where I was born one more time.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:40.310
It's something I absolutely need if I'm to win the Michelin three-star rating.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:45.270
Can you get back to your hotel on your own?

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:46.530
I'm fine!

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:48.570
Don't make fun of your mom!

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:50.440
Take care of yourself.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:51.190
Kojirou.

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:52.780
It was delicious.

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:01.410
Well, then.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:02.660
The new recipe competition!

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:04.670
I can't miss that!

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:06.540
I'm so lucky I could come today!

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:09.000
What I meant was, 
you should go home now.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.510
How can I go home after hearing
 about something like that?!

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:15.930
I can totally understand where 
Hinako's coming from, Shinomiya-san.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:18.240
Now that I've heard that Yukihira's joining the competition...

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:19.400
I want to see it too.

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:19.890
What?!

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:21.130
Right?!

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:25.020
In a sense, this is the first direct face-off between Yukihira-kun and Shinomiya-senpai!

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:28.480
It's a revenge match after 
the Cooking Battle at camp!

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:32.600
I just heard "Cooking Battle at camp."

00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:36.980
I don't know what she's 
talking about, Chapelle-sensei.

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:39.470
Inui is probably tipsy.

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:41.910
She drank too much wine.

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:43.660
Hm, I see.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:47.440
The Tohtsuki inspector.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:50.510
So Yukihira Souma's dish 
tonight will determine

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:53.670
whether he'll pass the 
Stagiaire at this restaurant.

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:54.570
I see.

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:56.510
But the odds are rather 
stacked against him.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:57.840
Indeed.

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:03.520
Tohtsuki students typically learn the basics of French cuisine in the junior high division,

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:05.850
but he has no such experience.

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:09.190
Based on what I've seen in my class and Shinomiya's assignment during camp,

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:13.920
he seems to be able to handle recreating existing recipes without problems.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:17.610
But it's an entirely different matter
 to develop a new recipe from scratch.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:21.080
Not to mention, 
<i>he'll</i> be the one judging the dishes.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:22.040
Huh?

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:24.880
Are you participating in the competition too, Wei-san?

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:25.290
Yes.

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:29.920
Wei was the Chief Meat Chef
 at SHINO's until six months ago.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:31.630
I see.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.300
{Why'd you switch to being the manager of customer service?}Why switch to managing customer service?{what even is line length hello}

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:37.260
This competition was held several times a month at the flagship restaurant too.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:42.140
But my entry was used
only once in two years.

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:44.850
I thought I had to do something.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.440
I switched to customer service management

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:52.070
because I thought I'd learn something by interacting with our guests.

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:57.570
But I've never slacked on my daily training as a chef.

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:58.470
Me neither.

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:02.700
I have to show that I didn't 
become the Chief Meat Chef

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.540
just because Wei stepped aside.

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:09.540
Everyone's serious about 
the new recipe competition.

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:12.290
Do you have the resolve to take this on?

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:20.820
There's something I learned 
from listening to Shinomiya-senpai earlier.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:25.460
I'm only thinking about bringing that vision into reality right now.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:32.270
I'm going to put all of my resolve
 and stuff on a plate, so...

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:36.110
It's time.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:37.650
Start cooking.

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:38.860
Oui, Chef!

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:43.530
<i>Heat honey and sugar until the mixture reaches a deep golden color,</i>

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:47.330
<i>then simmer it down after adding 
Madeira wine, red wine, and fond de veau.</i>

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.960
<i>In the meantime, 
sautee ground chicken with butter,</i>

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:51.580
<i>then sweat the onions.</i>

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:58.320
<i>Hey, Dad.</i>

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:00.100
<i>Why do you grill fish like that?</i>

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:01.240
<i>Hm?</i>

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:04.510
<i>It's because the skin gets crispier this way.</i>

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:07.990
<i>Huh, there's a technique for that?</i>

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:10.630
<i>There's a lot to a diner.</i>

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:11.770
<i>Hm...</i>

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:13.100
<i>What?</i>

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:16.440
<i>Well, maybe that's good enough for now.</i>

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:22.280
<i>Souma-kun, can you tell me why you know French culinary techniques?</i>

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:26.160
<i>Oh, I learned this technique from my dad.</i>

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:29.910
<i>He said it's perfect for crisping up fish skin.</i>

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:33.670
<i>I can see now what Dad had built.</i>

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:36.880
<i>He'd consolidated all the experiences</i>

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:43.130
<i>he's had with different cultures, 
techniques, and impressions</i>

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:47.600
<i>into his skill set to create 
the ideal diner of his dreams!</i>

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:50.830
<i>In that case, what I should do...</i>

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:52.560
<i>is poêlé.</i>

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:53.560
<i>Suer.</i>

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:54.680
<i>Allumette.</i>

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:55.580
<i>Escalope...</i>

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:56.400
<i>Déglacer...</i>

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:57.160
<i>Ciseler...</i>

00:11:57.160 --> 00:11:57.830
<i>Rôti...</i>

00:11:57.830 --> 00:11:58.520
<i>Braiser...</i>

00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:18.500
<i>I'm going to shatter who I've been until now!</i>

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:41.320
We're now finished tasting the three dishes from Lucie-san, Wei-san, and Abel-san.

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:42.610
Yukihira!

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:43.700
You're last!

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.410
Aren't you done yet?!

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:52.540
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:00.670
A whole quail!

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:02.630
So fragrant!

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:05.880
Yukihira Souma, what is that dish?

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:08.010
Um, this is...

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:09.350
a chicken and egg rice bowl.

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:10.060
Huh?

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:11.600
Chicken and egg... rice bowl?

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:13.680
Oh, now that you mention it,

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:16.100
I guess this isn't in a rice bowl, like a donburi.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:18.560
But please just try it.

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:22.990
This is the best French 
dish I can serve right now.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:24.990
<i>Quail meat.</i>

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:30.200
<i>A common ingredient in France and Italy, not just in restaurants, but in homes.</i>

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:32.910
<i>Well, it certainly looks like a French dish...</i>

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.410
<i>...but a chicken and egg rice bowl?</i>

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:38.170
<i>So the quail and the poached egg are the chicken and egg from the name.</i>

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:40.540
<i>What's your trick, Yukihira?</i>

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:43.170
Let us have a taste.

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:46.380
<i>That dish means everything.</i>

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:49.850
<i>Can he impress Shinomiya Kojirou with it?</i>

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:53.350
<i>The Stagiaire system has a hidden true purpose.</i>

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:56.310
<i>Can Yukihira-kun actually meet its expectations?</i>

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:09.740
I'll try it too!

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.030
What's this?!

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:14.500
There's egg inside... and risotto too...

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:21.790
<i>So delicious!</i>

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:27.760
<i>The silky egg, quail meat, and rice intertwine in dynamic synergy!</i>

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:30.590
<i>What is this texture?</i>

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:33.640
The chicken and egg rice bowl consists of five main ingredients:

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:37.060
chicken meat, egg, rice, onions, and seasoned stock.

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:41.690
After searing the quail in some oil,
 it's been slowly rôti, or roasted, in the oven.

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:45.320
So it's crunchy on the surface and juicy underneath.

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:49.280
The egg was seasoned with 
salt and pepper for a little bite,

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:53.700
and then mixed with cream
 for an even richer texture.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:56.790
The creaminess of the poached egg is critical to this dish, after all.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:00.710
The risotto was finished with milk for mildness.

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:02.670
{To it, }I added ground chicken sauteed in butter,

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:06.880
and onions that were sweated 
for enhanced sweetness.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:11.300
The sauce consists of soy sauce
 added to Madeira,

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:12.850
lightly sweetened with sugar and honey.

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:16.810
Like seasoned stock, 
it brings the ingredients together.

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:20.060
In other words, this dish reconceptualized the chicken and egg rice bowl

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.520
using French culinary techniques.

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:26.860
<i>Yet, using something like risotto to stuff the quail</i>

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:29.490
<i>should've resulted in some leakage.</i>

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.820
Yukihira, how did you do the stuffing?

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:32.820
Oh!

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:33.990
The earlier texture!

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:36.240
I used cabbage.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:38.950
I wrapped the risotto in cabbage that'd been parboiled in salt water

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:40.710
before stuffing the quail.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.920
That's what you used in
 the Cooking Battle at camp!

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:48.380
<i>The chou farci that Shinomiya made then...</i>

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:50.760
<i>The cabbage's texture is perfect.</i>

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:53.090
<i>While retaining its crunchiness,</i>

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:56.220
<i>the process brought out its sweetness,</i>

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.060
<i>which serves to gently meld the flavors</i>

00:15:58.060 --> 00:15:59.890
<i>of the fragrant quail meat and the stuffing.</i>

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:04.060
<i>What the Academy wants to see in its students during the Stagiaire</i>

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:07.480
<i>is that they contribute something
 to a professional setting,</i>

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:10.150
<i>but the Stagiaire's true purpose goes beyond that.</i>

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:14.450
<i>After the war, young hopefuls seeking to become professional French chefs</i>

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.870
<i>migrated to France in droves.</i>

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:19.830
<i>They went from restaurant to restaurant</i>

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:24.290
<i>to observe legendary chefs at close range so that they could learn,</i>

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:26.500
<i>steal, and extract the techniques</i>

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:30.210
<i>and eventually build their own cooking.</i>

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:34.220
<i>Their blood, sweat, and tears</i>

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:38.140
<i>are what allowed true French cuisine to flourish in Japan today.</i>

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:44.350
<i>The Stagiaire's true purpose is to have students undergo
 what the young hopefuls of yore did time and time again.</i>

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:46.860
<i>What can they steal from the pros?</i>

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:50.070
You did it, Yukihira.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:56.200
Shinomiya-senpai, you said you came back to Japan so that you could reach greater heights in French cuisine.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:17:00.410
If that's the case, then what I'm supposed to be doing right now is the complete opposite.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:03.410
I'm going to break through the cooking
 I've been doing in the same environment

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:04.870
I was born into and grew up in.

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:09.590
This is my first dish as the new Yukihira.

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:12.920
<i>Now, it's time to judge.</i>

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:18.720
<i>Will Yukihira Souma's dish make it to SHINO's menu?</i>

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:26.730
No, it's too low-quality.

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:32.530
At least, if it stays what it is now.

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:37.530
It's fine enough to be served at some small-time restaurant you'll have in the future,

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:41.950
but it's a little lackluster to be served at Shinomiya Kojirou's restaurant.

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:43.290
But, still...

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:47.460
I could beat into you what I'd do
 if I were to make this dish.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:48.880
How about it?

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:51.630
Please do!

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:56.590
Listen, in this case, you'd use sherry vinegar.

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:59.550
Add red wine only after you've
 deglazed the pan with the vinegar.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:00.600
Got it.

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:02.560
Sherry vinegar is from Spain, huh.

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:04.220
Don't forget to skim the foam.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:05.230
Got it!

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:09.690
Yes, Yukihira Souma passed.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:16.450
Well, thanks so much for teaching me
 until the sun came up.

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:19.160
That's because you're such a slow learner.

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:21.490
Thank you, Master Shinomiya!

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:22.580
Stop it!

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:23.370
I'm no master.

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:23.990
Master!

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:25.080
He called you "master"!

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:27.500
You're so arrogant, letting
 someone call you "master."

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:28.370
Shut up!

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:29.500
I didn't make him do it!

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:31.130
You can be more honest.

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:32.500
Yeah, you're actually happy about it.

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:33.750
Oh.

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:35.670
Yukihira.

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:41.010
Grab the First Seat in the Tohtsuki Elite Ten.

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:42.510
Will do!

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:47.520
I wonder how many will survive this year's Stagiaire.

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:49.560
Along with the camp training,

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:53.020
it is where a large number of students are weeded out.

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:55.690
Only those who are willing to face their own limits

00:18:55.690 --> 00:19:01.030
and try to overcome them will grow and gain the fruits of their labor.

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:03.700
They are the Generation of Prodigies.

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:05.620
Next!

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:06.450
Don't stop!

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:08.000
Keep moving!

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:10.000
Yes, Kurokiba-san!

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:14.880
My delinquent son turned over a brand-new leaf.

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:15.920
Welcome!

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:18.130
You guys behave too!

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:20.090
Don't bother the other customers.

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:21.890
Yes, Kurokiba-san!

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:26.520
Aldini-kun, you should join in the new menu planning and development too.

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:28.520
Okay, thank you.

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:32.600
<i>I can't just keep lagging behind my brother.</i>

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:35.690
Cute, cute, nervous, nervous!

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:37.980
Cute, cute, nervous, nervous!

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:40.240
Excited, excited, sparkle, sparkle!

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:42.660
Excited, excited, sparkle, sparkle!

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:45.530
Turn delicious!

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:48.700
Turn delicious!

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:51.710
Enjoy, ladies.

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:54.130
Table 3 wants no onions and extra oil.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:55.670
{Table 8 wants extra large serving with less salt.}Table 8, extra large with less salt.

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:57.920
{Table 9 wants a normal serving with cabbage and roast pork on top, plus half a serving of rice.}Table 9, normal with cabbage,
roast pork, and a half serving of rice.

00:19:57.920 --> 00:19:59.550
{Table 11 wants hard noodles and extra bean sprouts!}Table 11, hard noodles, extra bean sprouts.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:01.260
{Table 12 needs a second serving of noodles, stat!}Another noodle serving
 for table 12, stat!

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:03.050
I'm not going to give up!

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:06.680
But, Ibusaki-kun... this restaurant's already...

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:08.850
Let me have the kitchen one last time!

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:12.810
I'm going to turn this around!

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:14.100
Are you sure?

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:16.020
You're going to take on serving the guests too?

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:18.230
You won't have the energy!

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:20.530
Please, let me try!

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:24.490
I want to be useful outside of the kitchen, as well!

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:26.450
Indeed.

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:29.910
You are worthy of receiving the knowledge

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:34.580
I have cultivated and honed
 of how to ignite the fire.

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:35.630
Okay!

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:38.710
Delicious!

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:41.170
I thought you were just 
two-bit characters at first glance,

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:42.550
but you have real skill!

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:44.090
Don't underestimate us!

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:46.180
We strike fear into people's hearts!

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:47.510
We are the Polar Star Force!

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:49.220
My!

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:51.520
To think there'd be so much less left over

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:53.690
just because we added just a touch of seasoning!

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:57.400
Yes, that's the power of spices.

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:02.110
Chef, I'd like to order another dish.

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:04.240
Is there anything you'd recommend?

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:08.780
Yes, there is something I'm confident you'll like.

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:13.160
It's Quail Stuffed with Risotto and Egg,
 Cheeky Youngster Style.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:20.630
I'm back!

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:23.550
Yukihira, so you're the first one back.

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:25.970
Oh, Fumio-san. It's been a while.

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:30.140
You're looking pretty good.

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:32.680
Here. You've received a lot of mail.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:33.680
Huh?

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:35.140
Whoa!

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:36.350
What's this?

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:38.980
They're all Cooking Battle challenges.

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:41.640
An intensely burning desire burst forth

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:41.640
seki wo kitta nodo kara te ga deru hodo

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:40.190
Excuse me!

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:42.110
So you're back, Yukihira Souma!

00:21:41.640 --> 00:21:47.360
But not from me, from someone else

00:21:41.640 --> 00:21:47.360
hoshiku nattan da boku ja nai betsu no dareka

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:45.400
I'm a second-year in high school named Kabutoyama Tetsuji!

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:47.360
I challenge you to a Cooking Battle. Please accept!

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:52.490
Where's the me who believed that

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:52.490
yume to kibou hoka ni nani ga iru to

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:52.490
You first-years are on the same playing field as us upperclassmen now.

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:57.530
All one needs is to have hopes and dreams

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:57.530
omoeta koro no boku wa ima izuko e

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:53.290
So—

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:54.200
Sure.

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:56.960
Let's do it now.

00:21:57.530 --> 00:22:02.790
Wrapped around something long, my compass was lost

00:21:57.530 --> 00:22:02.790
nagai mono ni makarete ushinatta michishirube

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:08.380
On the border of life and death, snow drops bloom

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:08.380
sei to shi no hazama ni wa sunoo duroppu ga sakimidareru

00:22:08.380 --> 00:22:13.840
If by some mistake they get smashed

00:22:08.380 --> 00:22:13.840
nanika no machigai de kudakechitte shimatta nara

00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:19.060
At least put flowers on the empty husk

00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:19.060
semete boku no nukegara ni hanataba wo soete

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:24.730
Is that the way things are? Yes, it is

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:24.730
konna mon ka na konna mon deshou

00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:29.860
You can call it resignation if you want

00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:29.860
akirame da to omowaretatte kamawanai kedo

00:22:29.860 --> 00:22:35.570
But that's not me, that's not me

00:22:29.860 --> 00:22:35.570
boku rashiku nai boku rashiku nai

00:22:35.570 --> 00:22:40.370
There's no value in something just anyone could make

00:22:35.570 --> 00:22:40.370
dare ni mo datte tsukureru mon ni kachi wa nai

00:22:48.920 --> 00:22:53.970
As I trace my fingers over the the scars

00:22:48.920 --> 00:22:53.970
ato ni natta kizuguchi wo nazori nagara

00:22:52.850 --> 00:22:53.970
Erina-sama.

00:22:53.970 --> 00:22:59.430
Something sleeping deep inside of me awakens

00:22:53.970 --> 00:22:59.430
yobisamasun da boku no fukaku nemuru nanika

00:22:57.890 --> 00:22:59.850
Welcome back, Hisako.

00:22:59.430 --> 00:23:04.350
If there was something like that, it would have long ago

00:22:59.430 --> 00:23:04.350
sonna mon ga areba tokku no tou ni

00:23:02.360 --> 00:23:04.400
It's <i>Cooking Battle Flash News</i>...

00:23:04.350 --> 00:23:09.730
Melded into this world like a chameleon

00:23:04.350 --> 00:23:09.730
kamereon mitai ni kono sekai ni somatteru

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:06.780
Yukihira Souma!

00:23:07.530 --> 00:23:12.320
I want to cram as much knowledge and as many techniques into me as I can and keep battling at the Academy.

00:23:09.730 --> 00:23:12.360
Do I live as if I'm already dead?

00:23:09.730 --> 00:23:12.360
shinda you ni ikite iru

00:23:12.360 --> 00:23:14.860
Am I dead but still as if alive?

00:23:12.360 --> 00:23:14.860
ikita you ni shinde iru

00:23:13.070 --> 00:23:15.450
I wanna keep throwing everything I've got at cooking.

00:23:14.860 --> 00:23:20.410
On the border of life and death, the snow drops are so beautiful

00:23:14.860 --> 00:23:20.410
sei to shi no hazama ni aru sunoo duroppu wa sou kirei da

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:20.170
There will be plenty of suitable fodder for you to use and grow.

00:23:20.170 --> 00:23:23.840
That's the kind of place Tohtsuki Academy is.

00:23:20.410 --> 00:23:25.500
There's no sense in starting something if you're going to give up

00:23:20.410 --> 00:23:25.500
akirameru kurai nara saisho kara yaranai yo

00:23:25.500 --> 00:23:36.010
Amidst the snow drops, turn pure white once again

00:23:25.500 --> 00:23:28.380
sunoo duroppu no naka de

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:36.010
mou ichido masshiro ni somare

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:40.760
Me, and the other me

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:40.760
boku to boku yo

00:23:43.190 --> 00:23:44.270
Glad you liked it!

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:49.940
Hey, to everyone here:

00:23:49.940 --> 00:23:54.910
I'll accept any challenge at any time from anyone,

00:23:54.910 --> 00:23:57.410
so come at me whenever!

00:23:57.410 --> 00:24:00.410
Let's forget the formalities. 
We can get to it right now.

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:03.920
Let's have a Cooking Battle!

00:24:07.550 --> 00:24:09.550
Glad you liked it.
